 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 31,
   "y": 3,
   "text": "NORTH: Nant Ffrancon and Ogwen. Gogledd. The A5 carries on to Bethesda and the sea, and it is the route Telford built to get the mail to Holyhead."
  },
  {
   "x": 6,
   "y": 24,
   "text": "WEST: Pen-y-Pass and Yr Wyddfa. Gorllewin. The Miners' Track and the Pyg Track both start a mile up the road. Nobody agrees on why the second one is called Pyg."
  },
  {
   "x": 9,
   "y": 30,
   "text": "CRIB GOCH. 'Red ridge'. A knife edge of rock on the Snowdon Horseshoe that has made a great many brave people say a short word. Not a place for a first date."
  },
  {
   "x": 34,
   "y": 33,
   "text": "THE MINERS' TRACK. Copper miners walked this way to the mine under the mountain. It is now one of the easier ways up Yr Wyddfa, which is not the same thing as easy."
  },
  {
   "x": 17,
   "y": 27,
   "plaque": "pen_y_gwryd_everest",
   "title": "Everest, 1953",
   "text": "In 1953 the British team that was about to attempt Everest trained in these hills and stayed at the Pen-y-Gwryd Hotel. Their signatures are still on the ceiling of the smoke room, with the names of climbers who came after them. On 29 May Edmund Hillary and Tenzing Norgay reached the summit."
  },
  {
   "x": 38,
   "y": 34,
   "plaque": "pen_y_gwryd_causeway",
   "title": "The Llydaw Causeway",
   "text": "The causeway across Llyn Llydaw was built in 1853 for the Britannia copper mine, whose workings lie beneath the high lake Glaslyn. Ore came down in sledges and went on by cart and by water. Walkers took over the miners' track long ago, and the causeway has been getting more use since the mine closed than it ever did while the mine worked."
  },
  {
   "x": 44,
   "y": 24,
   "plaque": "pen_y_gwryd_dyli",
   "title": "Cwm Dyli",
   "text": "The power station at Cwm Dyli opened in 1906. Water piped from Llyn Llydaw falls the long way down the hillside to the turbines, and the station is one of the oldest hydroelectric stations in Britain that still works. It makes electricity without anybody remarking on it, which is the best kind."
  }
 ],
